{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be","id":1202695,"title":"Who will your next Dragon-Blooded PC be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-03T13:01:36-07:00","id":1202695,"title":"Who will your next Dragon-Blooded PC be?","content":"As we start to get a picture of the Dragon-Blooded in 3E and look forward to the mechanics, I wonder what sorts of Dragon-Blooded PCs people are interested in building and playing.<br /> <br /> Because I work in a field that involves a lot of NIMBY issues, I'm more interested in <b><i>what you actually intend you play</i></b> rather than things that you think might be interesting or that a buddy might play.<br /> <br /> Has the material released so far inspired you to make a particular terrestrial PC? Do you want to resurrect a 1E/2E PC in this new edition? Are you at all concerned that the fluff or mechanics won't support the kind of exalt that you want to make?<br /> <br /> Who will your next Dragon-Blooded PC be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:18:24-07:00","id":1202700,"title":"","content":"V'neef Lewen is the son from the male line of a Cadet House adopted into House V'neef, and an Exalted Patrician mother. A Spiral Academy graduate (and White Veil Stylist) he's married into House Sesus and has to prove himself worthy of trust by their spy network. Obviously betrayal of the House of his birth is the best way to do that.<br /> <br /> Of course, what's actually going on is that Exalted bloodline in the Patrician House his mother came from.... yeah.... it's Iselsi. He's been cleared to do anything and everything he has to do behind closed doors against House V'neef while cultivating relations with his father's House in public in order to prove himself to the Council of Masks. The goal of course is to get him as high as possible in the Sesus spy hierarchy to serve the interests of House Iselsi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:20:40-07:00","id":1202703,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I'm destined to be a Storyteller for life, but I'm curious to see what my players come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:06:48-07:00","id":1202755,"title":"","content":"Paper Daughters are amazing and I fully intend to play one if I ever get the chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:35:49-07:00","id":1202763,"title":"","content":"Assuming I ever get to play and it's a DB that I play, probably an Immaculate Monk who's goal is to become a Grand Master of the Immaculate Arts. So nothing special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:58:04-07:00","id":1202779,"title":"","content":"Seeing as my group will be playing a Tepet Campaign, I will likely play Sesus Wilar, AKA the Outcast &quot;Jester&quot;. A man who, with his wife, died along with the Tepet Legions, but unlike his unfortunate wife, he only died on paper. Being one of those rare couples that actually felt affection for each other he found far greater acceptance amongst his wife's family then his own, and seeing a grand opportunity for advancement within house Tepet in &quot;these troubled times&quot;, &quot;Jester&quot; has founded a mercenary company called &quot;The Scraps&quot; in the threshold. It's full of deserters, bandits, and thieves, but &quot;Jester&quot; is using his great personal skills, mastery of trade-craft, and business acumen, to make something worthy of them, and to find solutions for his adopted houses... problems... all while causing as many problems for house Sesus as he can in the process. He blames them personally for the loss of his wife, and will see the house burn to the ground, or die trying.<br /> <br /> Edit: 1 Bonus Point to anyone who can guess the main inspiration for my character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 04-03-2018, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:31:12-07:00","id":1202795,"title":"","content":"We are actually playing mortals right now that will exalt once we get all the chapters. I am playing a Prasadi Godblooded archer who still has good breeding from his fathers side. He is currently on a quest to 'awaken' his essence and explore the distant and 'exotic' homeland of his people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:48:57-07:00","id":1202802,"title":"","content":"What began as a joke is slowly becoming reality.<br /> <br /> Sooo, back when 3e core dropped, I had a look at the Merits, and found all sorts of wonderful NPC-giving merits! Then I got to thinking, what kind of a character would have ALL of them? (Well, Command dropped pretty soon once I realized military commander wasn't the style I wanna go for)<br /> <br /> Enter &quot;Cynis Cid&quot;, the DB pimp stacked with NPC merits. Allowed to remain unmarried due to House Cynis not wanting his bussiness going to the wife's house, he is a traveller through and through. So colourful and exotic is his caravan that they are often mistaken for a traveling circus. He always travels with his posse, which includes his loyal manservant, his bodyguards and of course his ladies of the night. They may be a posse, but to him they are a family and he will do anything to protect that. <br /> <br /> Haven't fleshed out the character that much more. Debating on should I make him a sorcerer (those Demons and Elementals bring out even more NPCs), or instead just focusing on native DB Brawl Charms. And yeah, in case you couldn't tell, he is to be played for laughs as a sympathetic pimp, not a realistic depiction at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T01:19:20-07:00","id":1202903,"title":"","content":"No idea whatsoever - have a bunch of leftover concepts from previous editions to play with i haven't touched in all too many months. That said i haven't read much on how things are turning out for the Chosen of the Dragons in 3e and it feels kind of unfair to the spirit of the thread to utterly ignore some of the new concepts and twists to just port over old ideas.<br /> <br /> That said, i do get tempted to make a play on both, by rehashing one of those unused characters as the survivor of some previous era awakening in the Time of Tumult from hibernation induced by one of the funky (never implemented) DB charm suggestions of the 1e Storyteller's Handbook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, could some charitable soul throw me some previews to look at? I would be most thankful for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-04-2018, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T09:46:33-07:00","id":1203043,"title":"","content":"The real question is, which kind of DB game is it? There are so many potential campaign ideas, and character ideas underneath them, that are jumping out at me.<br /> <br /> I have to say, one thing this editions text on the DB has done well that other editions hasn't, is really driving home the matriarchal nature of the Realm. I don't really have any qualms playing a cis-female character (being cis-male myself), but I'd want to mix it up occasionally, and the RP potential of being married into another house are interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:32:43-07:00","id":1203102,"title":"","content":"Kaila, Fire-aspected outcaste mercenary, whose mercenary company specializes in dealing with undead infestations from local shadowlands. This will almost certainly lead her to bite off way more than she can chew. This will almost certainly get her killed.<br /> <br /> This will almost certainly be a fight worth fighting for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T18:45:29-07:00","id":1203228,"title":"","content":"Cathak Chiheshi is the youngest and likely to be the last of Cathak Cainan's children. At the House of Bells, she studied logistics and what another place and era would call 'hearts and minds' methods, and spent her Sabbatical in Jiara mastering the art of dance, which she had always loved. The last days of the Empress's reign saw her assigned as an officer of the garrison of the Kingdom of Sieversi, and as the longtime Ledaal governor of that satrapy lives out her last days, Cainan has ordered his daughter to see to it that she, or another member of their house, replaces the woman as Satrap.<br /> <br /> Personally, Chiheshi is slimmer and less amazonian than expected of her house, but like most dancers is made entirely out of silk and steel springs.Her skin is fair and her eyes and long flowing hair are the pale gray of wood ash; her aspect marking appears when her hair is struck by a strong breeze, stoking each strand like a hot coal. The same thing happens to hair and eyes alike when her anima flares, while her skin is surrounded by an almost invisible heat haze.<br /> <br /> I haven't <i>quite</i> nailed down her combat style, yet - I know that she's a martial artist and I'll have her use whatever lets me get her capoeira on best, but what that'll turn out to be is still undetermined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T23:40:38-07:00","id":1203310,"title":"","content":"Peleps Tanegar, swashbuckler of the Inner Sea!<br /> <br /> Intimacies include:<br /> Defining: Adventure! [I'm Exalted, motherfucker, I wasn't born to hold down a desk.]<br /> Major: Food! [Holy shit, this is delicious! What did you say it's called?]<br /> Major: Sex! [In the Dragons' Names, did you see the thighs on that girl?!]<br /> Minor: House Peleps [*sigh* Yes, mother, I'll keep an eye out for opportunities to advance the House's interests.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T01:11:06-07:00","id":1203321,"title":"","content":"Alexia is the only daughter of a very wealthy Patrician family, who exalted in primary school while being bullied by Dynast scions. Growing up, she had always heard that her family was descended from a Tepet general\u2019s tryst with a mortal woman (Alexia\u2019s grandmother), but being just mortals there was no way to prove the claim. Alexia\u2019s exaltation changed that, and so the family quietly adopted her as an outcaste to avoid a political scandal at the time. Forced to leave her mortal family to join her Exalted one, Alexia was always more than a little conflicted about being shuffled around because of politics that happened generations ago. She was ecstatic to actually meet her grandfather though before she went to Pasiap\u2019s Stair. It was during her time at the secondary school that the Tepet legions were destroyed by the Bull in the North and the perfidious actions of the other Great Houses. Upon graduating, she was given her grandfather\u2019s heirloom daiklave as well as a hastily penned letter from him. It extolled her to redeem the blade\u2019s honor by avenging him against the enemies of the Realm both inside and out. Alexia is conflicted about being treated like the weapon that she wields and the greater duty that her exaltation demands.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking that any socially savvy Dynast who meets Alexia will pretty quickly realize that she is way too familiar with life on the Blessed Isle to be an outcaste. While House Tepet has lost a lot more than political reputation, they certainly don\u2019t want Alexia\u2019s family history revealed as it might damage their already very tenuous attempts to get any marriage offers. While the house elders have forbidden her from seeing her mortal family, she stills sneaks out to visit them occasionally when she has the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T03:58:57-07:00","id":1203358,"title":"","content":"Well, it wont be my next DB character, since I'll nevsr be in a game, but I'd love to do something unusual, like a beatman Dragon Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T04:35:47-07:00","id":1203363,"title":"","content":"I've been wanting to play an earth-aspected magistrate who travels from town to town solving crimes and smashing heads. So that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:30:06-07:00","id":1203822,"title":"","content":"Cathak Nemis, a Fire Aspect swordswoman who uses the doctrine of House Cathak to temper her relentless bloodlust, forcing herself into the role of &quot;soldier&quot; when among her fellow soldiers, but unleashing her more unhinged, bloodthirsty side when things have broken down and they just need everything even remotely near her <i>dead. </i>Torn between her inherent bloodlust and her desire to be, in her own words, &quot;a warrior, not a murderer&quot;. Trained at the House of Bells, where she accidentally killed a classmate during a spar when she went overboard. Will be a fun exploration of the the dynamic between the forced order of The Realm and the intense emotions found in the Dragon Bloods, especially Fire Aspects. Also she's got a cool Red Jade Daiklave with with a bit of Soulsteel mixed in, whose charms will be based around aggression, speed, and relentlessness, with an aspect of it being a small to medium power boost (balance in the works) based on how much blood she's spilled. Fighting style overall is going to be somewhat akin to the Odogaron from MHW, lots of leaps and charges, and just generally an all out offensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:24:34-07:00","id":1203844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1203822#post1203822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cathak Nemis, a Fire Aspect swordswoman who uses the doctrine of House Cathak to temper her relentless bloodlust, forcing herself into the role of &quot;soldier&quot; when among her fellow soldiers, but unleashing her more unhinged, bloodthirsty side when things have broken down and they just need everything even remotely near her <i>dead. </i>Torn between her inherent bloodlust and her desire to be, in her own words, &quot;a warrior, not a murderer&quot;. Trained at the House of Bells, where she accidentally killed a classmate during a spar when she went overboard. Will be a fun exploration of the the dynamic between the forced order of The Realm and the intense emotions found in the Dragon Bloods, especially Fire Aspects. Also she's got a cool Red Jade Daiklave with with a bit of Soulsteel mixed in, whose charms will be based around aggression, speed, and relentlessness, with an aspect of it being a small to medium power boost (balance in the works) based on how much blood she's spilled. Fighting style overall is going to be somewhat akin to the Odogaron from MHW, lots of leaps and charges, and just generally an all out offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dunno when/if I'll have a chance, but I'm totally stealing her as an NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:39:57-07:00","id":1203849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1203822#post1203822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cathak Nemis, a Fire Aspect swordswoman who uses the doctrine of House Cathak to temper her relentless bloodlust, forcing herself into the role of &quot;soldier&quot; when among her fellow soldiers, but unleashing her more unhinged, bloodthirsty side when things have broken down and they just need everything even remotely near her <i>dead. </i>Torn between her inherent bloodlust and her desire to be, in her own words, &quot;a warrior, not a murderer&quot;. Trained at the House of Bells, where she accidentally killed a classmate during a spar when she went overboard. Will be a fun exploration of the the dynamic between the forced order of The Realm and the intense emotions found in the Dragon Bloods, especially Fire Aspects. Also she's got a cool Red Jade Daiklave with with a bit of Soulsteel mixed in, whose charms will be based around aggression, speed, and relentlessness, with an aspect of it being a small to medium power boost (balance in the works) based on how much blood she's spilled. Fighting style overall is going to be somewhat akin to the Odogaron from MHW, lots of leaps and charges, and just generally an all out offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soulsteel doesn't usually go well with the Chosen of Dragons if i got stuff from AotC right, but maybe that accenting makes things even more appropriate in the case of this unruly, hungry flame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:49:22-07:00","id":1203918,"title":"","content":"Outcaste heiress to a small kingdom that was usurped by a family member. Escaped with another character's (our eclipse) circus. Now she hides in plain sight as a show on the circus where using smoke and mirrors and some use of fire powers (namely in the assumption that one fire anima power is still going to be immunity to nonmagical fire) as the circuses amazing &quot;dragon blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> So a Fire aspect, pretending to be a human who pretends to be a fire aspect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:42:20-07:00","id":1203974,"title":"","content":"Injira, an Air Aspect Lost Egg of Prasad turned battle-sorcerer. He is, by many metrics, an ideal soldier; taking the coin and seeing the machine of the Realm convinced him it was the greatest force for civilization in the world, and he is fanatically loyal to the Throne; if ordered, he would happily lead a raid against his own homeland to preserve the Empire. He is sometimes known as the Spell-Terrier due to his personal loyalty to Mnemon, who has a daughter who was his tutor in sorcery (and not coincidentally, a Realm patriot herself); it was originally an insult given his small size and love of small canines (he <i>somehow</i> talked the instructors to let him bring his pet domestic fox along as a familiar), but he's embraced the term; he sees himself as a loyal hound meant to serve as an advance force to chase rats out of their dens by shouting his magics into the world.<br /> <br /> Many metrics. The others are aware his blood brother, who he adores, is a Lunar Anathema with an actual dog totem (my other character idea). One who is still sane, unlike those <i>other </i>Lunars who have been consumed by the beast within, and working very hard to control his instincts towards destruction and domination, but he's still a shapeshifter with a big silver tattoo on his head. He was quite shocked and unnerved when he discovered the mainstream Immaculates think of them as pure monsters incapable of getting on the path back into karma and harmony. He doesn't bring it up, but he quietly pressures his men and fellows to maybe judge people based on their actions as people. He'll assist the shikari, but he runs as an impartial magistrate who judges whether someone should be executed or shipped off to Prasad for purification and a second chance.<br /> <br /> Which is, naturally, what the Silver Pact wants - they almost planned it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-06-2018, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T18:50:40-07:00","id":1204064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1202779#post1202779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as my group will be playing a Tepet Campaign, I will likely play Sesus Wilar, AKA the Outcast &quot;Jester&quot;. A man who, with his wife, died along with the Tepet Legions, but unlike his unfortunate wife, he only died on paper. Being one of those rare couples that actually felt affection for each other he found far greater acceptance amongst his wife's family then his own, and seeing a grand opportunity for advancement within house Tepet in &quot;these troubled times&quot;, &quot;Jester&quot; has founded a mercenary company called &quot;The Scraps&quot; in the threshold. It's full of deserters, bandits, and thieves, but &quot;Jester&quot; is using his great personal skills, mastery of trade-craft, and business acumen, to make something worthy of them, and to find solutions for his adopted houses... problems... all while causing as many problems for house Sesus as he can in the process. He blames them personally for the loss of his wife, and will see the house burn to the ground, or die trying.<br /> <br /> Edit: 1 Bonus Point to anyone who can guess the main inspiration for my character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm probably wrong but my first thought was of Clay from The Losers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T19:46:30-07:00","id":1204078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KFinigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1204064#post1204064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably wrong but my first thought was of Clay from The Losers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read that series, but I think I'll look into it. Most of the inspiration for my character comes from the main character in the Phule's Company series: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phule&#39;s_Company_%28series%29\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phule&amp;#39;...y_%28series%29</a> the rest is from my interest in the Agent gone &quot;native&quot; concept, and trying to integrate the character into the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 04-06-2018, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T23:25:05-07:00","id":1204115,"title":"","content":"Currently torn between Realm and Lookshy. Ever since our group laid hands on that beautiful cloth map from the core KS, we've been itching for a military/geopolitical style campaign. Our group has had our fill of what that looks like as Solars from our time in 2E. However, both the challenges and the opportunities unique to the splat have become far more interesting to me since we first caught wind of 3E.<br /> <br /> With the removal of magitech and addition of recent stretch goal bonuses I am both eager and anxious to see the new form of 3E Lookshy. As far as the Realm, I have a net neutral outlook on the changes this go around in terms of swaying this decision. I will say the things I dislike, I don't feel as strongly about as the things I do like. Though the prospect of possibly actually getting to play on the Blessed Isle itself instead of dominantly in the Threshold is the most novel draw right now.<br /> <br /> Worth noting, given that our last campaign was in Champoor as Solars, I'd want to avoid Prasad given bad experiences with how that campaign progressed.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for character, since I've been anticipating a Realm campaign, probably a Water Aspect Martial Artist seeking to one day become a master and instructor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","user":"Aredin","date":". 04-07-2018, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:59:57-07:00","id":1204209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1203849#post1203849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soulsteel doesn't usually go well with the Chosen of Dragons if i got stuff from AotC right, but maybe that accenting makes things even more appropriate in the case of this unruly, hungry flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonbloods are disonant with artifacts that are primarily Soulsteel, this only has a relatively small amount in it, absorbing blood to grant the daiklave more power, similar to Steel Devil's charge mechanic. AotC specifically mentions that artifacts can use more than one magical material, with the primary one having the biggest influence on themes and deciding resonance. So the blood theme of Soulsteel will be secondary to the violence theme of Red Jade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T12:19:17-07:00","id":1204252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1204209#post1204209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dragonbloods are disonant with artifacts that are primarily Soulsteel, this only has a relatively small amount in it, absorbing blood to grant the daiklave more power, similar to Steel Devil's charge mechanic. AotC specifically mentions that artifacts can use more than one magical material, with the primary one having the biggest influence on themes and deciding resonance. So the blood theme of Soulsteel will be secondary to the violence theme of Red Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the fact Soulsteel enters as a secondary ingredient is the main reason i spoke of it as &quot;accenting&quot; things in an appropriate manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T23:58:44-07:00","id":1205113,"title":"","content":"Well, i think i have a character idea of my own to toy with now. It hinges on 3e's core stuff than anything else and truth be told is more of a build than concept, but it's a start.<br /> <br /> Basically, i decided to make a character that goes total nuts with the whole nature/poison theme: Wood Aspect trained in the Immaculate Style of his element, with Sorcery - and Wood Dragon's Claw as control spell - for a bonus. My intention is to see how far i can go in comboing/theming with mixing Wood Dragon Style charms, sorcerous Evocations from Wood Dragon's Claw, his anima and other native charms.<br /> <br /> My initial image of him was of a sort of rogue monk, something like an early Cevis Gandharva of the Forest Witches, a sort of youthful Thulsa Doom/Kurtz mix, but somewhere along the way i started thinking of him as a Outcaste and things changed into more group-friendly and interesting direction, a sort of Mowgli/Sun Wukong mix instead:<br /> <br /> A rural bumpkin that exalted in the middle of nowhere in the hinterlands of the Blessed Isle (probably, though Threshold in a strongly Immaculate-influenced Satrapy might work too), went into a kind of serious trip, half mystical revelation, half essence fever in action and buried/lost himself amidst the woods from there, wandering, foraging, meditating, hunting &amp; frolicking with dragons only knows what and finding a sort of illumination (sorcerous initiation) along the way and while living of the land for many months, if not a whole year or more, until growing rumors of his many and strange antics lead to the coming of one or more monks, under the mistaken assumption some rogue nature spirit was behind these actions.<br /> <br /> The monks, between amused, flabbergasted and shocked at the peculiar &quot;savage enlightened child&quot; took him to the Cloister of Wisdom - coin?choice?what? - where it was fully indoctrinated into proper immaculate ways, though the &quot;proper&quot; part itself (or the ascetism) never meshed well with his temperament, with lots of highs, lows and twists in the form of occasional bouts of rebellion, with and without sorcerous antics resulting from it. But the monks were patient, stern and unyielding, while Wood changes and adapts, so it was that he learned - to disguise well the sybaritic aspects that come all too naturally to his element, if not much else - until the time came for him to be unleashed upon Creation.<br /> <br /> ....ok, maybe Kasif/Jack Harkness hybrid - with Sorcery - might be a better description of him in the end. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Anyways, that's the DB PC that i intend to play next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-10-2018, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:34:50-07:00","id":1205174,"title":"","content":"Depends entirely on who runs the game, but if the guy who ran the last DB game decides to continue his previous story:<br /> <br /> Mnemon Aliden, the son of the Windtamer and an unknown mother, was given to House Mnemon to raise as part of a deal (which only the GM knows the details of). Aliden is an Air Aspect of slightly above average height, with pale blue skin, short white hair (which is not so much styled as it is windswept) and his iconic anima banner is that of a thundercloud, writhing with energy. His voice, while melodious, has been tamed and focused by years of study at the House of Bells to be almost as much of a weapon as his blue jade daiklave &quot;Stormfang&quot;. This blade is in the shape of a lightning bolt's outline, hosts an Elemental Lens, and allows it's wielder to absorb lightning into Essence - which Aliden usually throws out immediately as Elemental Bolts because he likes being a conduit for his element.<br /> <br /> He's never met his father, but as most of his peers don't have a close bond with theirs either it's mostly a matter of curiosity than anything else although he would pay almost any price to know who his mother is. He knows he isn't a child of House Mnemon thanks to a slip from his adopted mother, but he has been at first discouraged, then forbidden, and finally sorcerously bound against pestering any of his house elders about it.<br /> <br /> Aliden has three major problems in his future<ul><li>Firstly, the world doesn't live up to the standards he expects of it. He's old enough to remember how things worked under the Empress, but young enough to still be idealistic, and so is disgusted at the infighting among his elders when the world is going to crap. He doesn't have the wisdom to see that this is a flaw in how the Empress set everything up, and so idolises her.</li> <li>Secondly, he's only 21 and has no idea how to go about fixing things except with a blade or a pretty smile. He's been coasting on natural talent for the last 16 years, so one day he's going to get a rude awakening when he first experiences failure.</li> <li>Lastly, one of his hearthmates is addicted to crack cocaine and another is being slowly driven insane by an artifact cloak (and was a kleptomaniac even before this happened). He's too idealistic to realise his close friends have a problem they can't solve by themselves, and they won't ask for help.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13646,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","user":"realitycheque","date":".  Forgot the name of his dad. 04-12-2018, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:36:06-07:00","id":1205256,"title":"","content":"Windrider? Ain't that some demon related to the parentage of someone among the Ledaal? Or do you mean the ghost of whoever is buried in the Crypt/major eastern shadowland of the same name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:01:27-07:00","id":1205538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1205256#post1205256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Windrider? Ain't that some demon related to the parentage of someone among the Ledaal? Or do you mean the ghost of whoever is buried in the Crypt/major eastern shadowland of the same name?</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be misremembering the name, but I meant the old Air Aspected DB who is super in tune with the wind, I think he was mentioned in the old Air aspect book from 1E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:29:58-07:00","id":1205548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1205538#post1205538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be misremembering the name, but I meant the old Air Aspected DB who is super in tune with the wind, I think he was mentioned in the old Air aspect book from 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tepet Arada, the Wind-Dancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T07:41:15-07:00","id":1205587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1205548#post1205548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tepet Arada, the Wind-Dancer.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1205538#post1205538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be misremembering the name, but I meant the old Air Aspected DB who is super in tune with the wind, I think he was mentioned in the old Air aspect book from 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Cynis Mond, the Windtamer, awesome cloudcuckoolander genius and another elder Air Aspect from the same book.<br /> With a most interesting cross-edition easter egg/memetic mutation, might be said.<br /> <br /> Aspectbook: Air present us with the Crosswind Techniques, a group of Charms predicated on emulating and channeling Essence in a manner similar to the Essence within the very wind, first taught centuries ago by the eccentric innovator, \u201cWindtamer\u201d Cynis Mond (who no longer teaches the Techniques), that claimed to have created them as by-products of his other studies of the Essence of the winds.<br /> <br /> In 2e Crosswind Offense makes a comeback in Scroll of the Monk as the opening charm of Night Breeze Style, an air aspected stealth &amp; assassin-minded martial arts style. And the other opening charm, Shepherd the Leaf and Wind Needle Training are pretty obviously Crosswind Feint and Crosswind Empowerment Technique under new names. Could this have something to do with why he has stopped teaching them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T23:46:55-07:00","id":1205953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1203363#post1203363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wanting to play an earth-aspected magistrate who travels from town to town solving crimes and smashing heads. So that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm still not clear on who exactly becomes magistrates. Is it exclusively Pasiap's Stair graduates? Or, if someone thoroughly trained in law by the Spiral Academy is viable, how did the Empress deal with House-loyalties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T01:57:06-07:00","id":1205967,"title":"","content":"That Sobriquet Merit, though...<br /> <br /> Two women faced each other beneath the boughs of a peach tree. Each wore a sword, but neither had yet drawn. Cathak Yelena gripped her scabbard in her left hand, the hilt of her blade in her right. Her skin was stony grey, and her hair the deep brown of rich loam. Her eyes were clear and hard as diamonds.<br /> <br /> Tepet Araun's hands rested, seemingly casually, on her own hilt and scabbard. Her hair, the pale violet-white of a lightning bolt, was bound up and held in place with two sticks. Her skin was as white and unblemished as newfallen snow; her eyes, the cloudy grey of solid ice.<br /> <br /> Both women stood straight, apparently relaxed. Araun noted the slight tightness around Yelena's mouth, and the tension in her shoulders. <i>Her discipline is not as firm as she thinks,</i> Araun thought. Yelena shifted her grip fractionally. <i>Here it comes.</i><br /> <br /> Tepet Araun inhaled.<br /> <br /> No one, not any of the onlookers, not even Cathak Yelena, saw the strike. In one instant, Tepet Araun stood with her blade sheathed; in the next, she held it high, adding a flick of her wrist to the end of the motion to clean the sword of blood. Yelena crumpled to the ground, her eyes already empty.<br /> <br /> Tepet Araun exhaled.<br /> <br /> &quot;NOOOOOOOO!&quot; Cathak Khalid, Yelena's husband, burst from the crowd of onlookers and flung himself across his wife's body, wailing with grief. A single tear ran down Araun's cheek, leaving a trail of frost flowers in its wake: another challenger proven unworthy. She turned to go.<br /> <br /> &quot;Monster!&quot; Khalid hurled the familiar imprecation at Araun's back. Tepet Araun, known throughout the Realm and Threshold as the Winter Razor, kept walking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T03:06:34-07:00","id":1205976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1205953#post1205953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not clear on who exactly becomes magistrates. Is it exclusively Pasiap's Stair graduates? Or, if someone thoroughly trained in law by the Spiral Academy is viable, how did the Empress deal with House-loyalties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going on past canon, it was the Empress' direct appointment, so magistrates were handpicked for loyalty to the Realm. Probably the most famous canonical magistrate is Tepet Elana, a soldier who had no past experience with law. I think Fokuf/the Deliberative can appoint new magistrates, but aren't, and thus other power groups are hunting them down... IDR how much of that is still true, but hey, that's how I remember it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to who I'd play... varies on game, but I'm thinking my Outcaste bandit, Scrags, is probably gonna be my first choice. Short, destructive and in this for a good time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T07:42:33-07:00","id":1206020,"title":"","content":"I am thinking of a scion of a Tepet noble and the Lookshy House of the founder of Lookshy. They trained in both places, and is now the key between Tepet and Lookshy, as a potential alliance. Either sitting on the realm, and recreating the shogunate, or setting up a mini-empire.<br /> <br /> Sesus Azula.... don't have more, but that one is tempting xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T08:43:52-07:00","id":1206036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1205587#post1205587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Cynis Mond, the Windtamer, awesome cloudcuckoolander genius and another elder Air Aspect from the same book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the dude! I shall edit my post, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:32:03-07:00","id":1206046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206036#post1206036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the dude! I shall edit my post, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know it helped - and maybe pass that other stuff on the Crosswinds Techniques to your ST, just to see what might come out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:52:52-07:00","id":1206082,"title":"","content":"Cynis Erina, who was originally my first Dragon-Blood character and first Exalted character. I never got to properly update her to 2e because the 2e dragon-blood book was cancerously terrible. <br /> <br /> She's (probably - have to consider the new charmset in full first) an Air aspect, like her closest Exalted relatives, her aunt Cynis Beryl and her maternal grandmother*. While her own mother came from well -husbanded Essence, she never Exalted, and she was paired of with a boy from a rising patrician house suffering from an unfortunate lack of female heirs. Erina's mother had a dangerous habit of needling her sister about her family being more successful in business, and one night her parents died in a tragic accident. Her aunt adopted her -though mainly for the sake of her inheritance - and treated her as little more than a spare child in comparison to her spoiled, thus-far only son Dorim, who was expected to Exalt while she of course was not. <br /> <br /> *Also her blood father, Tepet Palim, her aunt's late husband. Fortunately for Erina, her aunt doesn't know. His mother, Tepet Mailin, is who eventually told Erina. <br /> <br /> She Exalted fairly ahead of the normal curve in primary school, so that flipped the relationship. It was surprising, but less so given she actually got her unfaithful uncle's progenerative Essence instead of Dorim. Suddenly she was Beryl's favored daughter, and her aunt revealed that she was actually a spy and assassin for the house rather than having much direct participation in business ventures. In addition to her normal training at the Spiral Academy, Erina learned violence and tradecraft which she took to enthusiastically. <br /> <br /> Then her shit of a cousin finally Exalted - unusually late, already in secondary school, but still Beryl wasted no time in favoring him again despite him being a boy (and a dumbass). When she graduates, it's clear that Beryl intends to get her stuck managing her parents' business instead of anything exciting. So while her aunt is away negotiating marriage, she slips into her aunt's secret rooms and steals her skycutter and a mask of disguise (I think that used to be a somewhat standardized artifact) and, while there, finds Beryl's ledger with a note about killing her sister and brother-in-law. So she sets out into the Threshold, seeking to make her own fortune and hopefully a Hearth that she can convince to come home and kill her aunt eventually. <br /> <br /> In play, she's mainly sneaky and talky, a Jane Bond sort with a similar taste for luxuries (and women). <br /> <br /> She might use White Veil instead of or with Thrown, depending on how that is. <br /> <br /> When I'll actually get to play her, I haven't a clue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:44:09-07:00","id":1206131,"title":"","content":"I have the curse of the Forever ST, so I don't foresee a DB PC in my near future. That said, reading the available material has given me an idea for an NPC in my game, so my experiments with DB creation will probably be fleshing out the renegade Dynastic scion who betrayed his house during the fall of Thorns and now leads a Mask of Winters aligned mercenary group called the Sickles of Thorns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T14:17:45-07:00","id":1206161,"title":"","content":"How's this for a concept: Fire Aspected knife-fighter?<br /> <br /> I wss thinking a fire aspected anima would go great with an up close and dirty fughting style. So he'd carry a short sword/daiklaive and an assortment of knives and daggers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:23:55-07:00","id":1206192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206082#post1206082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then her shit of a cousin finally Exalted - unusually late, already in secondary school, but still Beryl wasted no time in favoring him again despite him being a boy (and a dumbass).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the shit of a cousin's defense, if he was in secondary school <b>without </b>having already exalted, dumbass he's most definitely not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now her aunt, giving Erina the cold shoulder <b>after</b> having taught violence, business &amp; spycraft, is a whole different story... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T20:35:35-07:00","id":1206258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206020#post1206020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sesus Azula.... don't have more, but that one is tempting xD</div> </div> </div> </div>To capture the character she still needs to be of pretty high birth - I'm thinking most recent daughter of Sesus Raenyah and Oban?<br /> <br /> I'd use normal character creation rules, but have her still be a teenager, to reflect her being a prodigie. Officially she graduated early from the Cloister of Wisdom (of course she wouldn't have &quot;graduated early&quot; if they had any desire in trying to nurture her spiritual learning, but they wanted her the hell out of there!), and then &quot;vacationed&quot; at the Silken Diamond. Fire Dragon Stylist shikari wielding the Air-version of Elemental Bolt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T22:42:04-07:00","id":1206289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206192#post1206192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the shit of a cousin's defense, if he was in secondary school <b>without </b>having already exalted, dumbass he's most definitely not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now her aunt, giving Erina the cold shoulder <b>after</b> having taught violence, business &amp; spycraft, is a whole different story... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not one of the Big 4, one of the lesser &quot;Outer Coil&quot; mentioned that mortal Patricians and Dynasts go to. Of course, it's all from Erina's perspective, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T02:13:37-07:00","id":1206351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206258#post1206258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To capture the character she still needs to be of pretty high birth - I'm thinking most recent daughter of Sesus Raenyah and Oban?<br /> <br /> I'd use normal character creation rules, but have her still be a teenager, to reflect her being a prodigie. Officially she graduated early from the Cloister of Wisdom (of course she wouldn't have &quot;graduated early&quot; if they had any desire in trying to nurture her spiritual learning, but they wanted her the hell out of there!), and then &quot;vacationed&quot; at the Silken Diamond. Fire Dragon Stylist shikari wielding the Air-version of Elemental Bolt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh... nice concept. I haven't thought too much about it... Fire Aspect, Social primary, physical secondary, mental secondary perhaps... not 100% sure on this, but it's an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T02:54:55-07:00","id":1206353,"title":"","content":"If I were ever playing in a DB game I'd love to play one of the Wanasaan. I'm hoping we'll get to know them more in the Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:54:15-07:00","id":1206480,"title":"","content":"Was looking through Arms, musing about a Wood Aspect DB character whan I came across the hearthstone Gem of the Shield-Sister Tree, which combos awesomely with Arbor Sentinel Technique, Choose a hill, turret down and rain death. Sounds like a fun plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T10:54:19-07:00","id":1206527,"title":"","content":"Ledaal Shusha\u00efn (to be confirmed as I read carefully the houses' details), Fire Aspect, wielder of Rainmaker. Travels [campaign's direction], accompanied by her loyal mortal slave/friend/packmule/sidekick, [name to be decided], investigating menaces to Creation. Her real mission though is to take away the Nightmare Shard from the Nellens, for they can't be trusted not to use the dreaded artifact or guard it with the proper precaution.<br /> Noble, controlled heroine, not entirely unlike the archetype of a 19th-century gentleman explorer.<br /> Well, that's the idea, anyway. In practice, things burn or explode and Shusha\u00efn's got to make herself and her house look better by talking (or punching) to the right people and pretend everything went as expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","user":"ChairKicker","date":". 04-13-2018, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T11:31:22-07:00","id":1206539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206527#post1206527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shusha\u00efn Ledaal</div> </div> </div> </div>surname first","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T11:44:18-07:00","id":1206544,"title":"","content":"My next DB is going to be, barring any significant changes, Mnemon Galdr, who's the daughter of one of Mnemon's various daughters, well regarded from her graduation at the Cloister of Wisdom, and devout enough she would've been a monk if not for the fact that there were those awkward celibacy vows and she actually enjoys sleeping on mattresses. <br /> <br /> Her main story hook is that her former personal maid and lover was murdered while she was off at school, and she doesn't know who did it, so she's somewhat flailing about given all her connections she made due to being actually <i>nice</i> to people, and valuing her friends as friends, not contacts. It's shielded her so far because she hasn't made many enemies, but hitting up on that big 21st year means stepping out into the real world now, whether her somewhat optimistic view of people is ready or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:42:34-07:00","id":1206588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206539#post1206539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> surname first</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, mistyped because I had the post window open first and decided on the given name after already typing her surname.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T20:50:38-07:00","id":1206780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206480#post1206480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was looking through Arms, musing about a Wood Aspect DB character whan I came across the hearthstone Gem of the Shield-Sister Tree, which combos awesomely with Arbor Sentinel Technique, Choose a hill, turret down and rain death. Sounds like a fun plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do i find this hearthstone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T06:19:40-07:00","id":1206864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206780#post1206780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do i find this hearthstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arrms of the Chosen, page 135","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:57:57-07:00","id":1206924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206289#post1206289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not one of the Big 4, one of the lesser &quot;Outer Coil&quot; mentioned that mortal Patricians and Dynasts go to. Of course, it's all from Erina's perspective, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Her attitude toward him while ignoring his mother's far greater failings gives off a bit of a &quot;the lady doth protest too much, methinks&quot;/tsundere vibe it feels, or maybe it's just me head playing tricks with smoke, who knows. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206864#post1206864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arrms of the Chosen, page 135</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, checking every Wood aspected/themed thing i can find to mine for options and combinations to go with my next character. Don't quite know what i'll actually use or not, but the more options/tools, the better for certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T22:04:21-07:00","id":1207540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1206924#post1206924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Her attitude toward him while ignoring his mother's far greater failings gives off a bit of a &quot;the lady doth protest too much, methinks&quot;/tsundere vibe it feels, or maybe it's just me head playing tricks with smoke, who knows. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. <br /> <br /> It's more dismissive prejudices at play. Her aunt only ever elevated her because her own boy was disappointly mortal, but of course once he finally Exalted he was much more important because he's her real son (and well bred) as opposed to (supposedly) being from barely better than patrician stock and of course she assumes Erina's still controllable because she's stayed in line all these years.<br /> <br /> Whereas Erina dismissed her cousin as worthy of considering a threat or obstacle because he's just a boy, and a late bloomer to boot. And of course she resents getting sidelined for someone with those shortcomings, but her murdery plans are focused on her aunt for that betrayal. Nor does she consider that he might have some legitimate grudges against her during the time she was the golden child. <br /> <br /> Blindspots all around, really. A backstory I hope an ST could mine for 'fun'.<br /> <br /> Ah, well. Someday...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 04-16-2018, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T22:19:20-07:00","id":1207544,"title":"","content":"Ledaal Ramana, Fire-Aspect emissary to Lookshy, mostly negotiated trade access to Nexus, coordinates Wyld Hunt cooperation, delivers threats against Lookshy extending aide to rebel satrapies, etc. Unofficially fanning the flames of the Purists behind closed doors with talk about how the Realm would never tolerate the rampant Hundred Gods Heresies through the River Province if there were a regime change in Lookshy willing to form a closer relationship with the Immaculate Order and the Legions...<br /> <br /> Working at very much cross purposes with her uncle Ledaal Rae, who wants to form an alliance with the current regime against Mask of Winter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T04:31:13-07:00","id":1207601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1207544#post1207544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ledaal Ramana, Fire-Aspect emissary to Lookshy, mostly negotiated trade access to Nexus, coordinates Wyld Hunt cooperation, delivers threats against Lookshy extending aide to rebel satrapies, etc. Unofficially fanning the flames of the Purists behind closed doors with talk about how the Realm would never tolerate the rampant Hundred Gods Heresies through the River Province if there were a regime change in Lookshy willing to form a closer relationship with the Immaculate Order and the Legions...<br /> <br /> Working at very much cross purposes with her uncle Ledaal Rae, who wants to form an alliance with the current regime against Mask of Winter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setup of agendas at potential conflict that can take some interesting challenges to balance out - or at least solve in a way that satisfy either Ledaal (or who knows, neither, Fate can bring surprises like that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T16:29:21-07:00","id":1209045,"title":"","content":"The Forest-Devil Mask makes me consider a Zorro type figure. A Dynast whose gone masked vigilante against the Realm to protect the subjugated populace of a satrapy, while maintaining their Dynast identity for intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-22-2018, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T20:18:05-07:00","id":1209106,"title":"","content":"There's some other builds that entertain me from a theorycrafting perspective, but the character I feel I'd be most likely to try to play is...<br /> <br /> Nellens Kiren is a thoroughly corrupt bureaucrat, and he doesn't even have the decency to be corrupt for the right <i>reasons</i>. Dismissive of his family after his grandmother married him into a patrician family wealthy enough to buy his entire sorry Dynastic household, he's decided that the only way he's ever going to earn the respect he deserves as a Prince of the Earth is to make himself richer than Ragara, one egregious embezzlement at a time.<br /> <br /> In a political game, he could stay in place, swayed for one reason or other to use his power of corruption to support the PCs' faction. In the probably-more-likely scenario where I end up in an action game, he could potentially tweak the wrong nose with some misdeed and end up effectively exiled to the Threshold, forced to mingle with, horror of horrors, <i>barbarians</i>.<br /> <br /> Of course, if he ever realizes that a Tengese peasant doesn't know the difference between a Nellens and a Mnemon, he might change his tune on barbarians right quick.<br /> <br /> Probably a Water Aspect (though Fire with Water-y tendencies is possible), Bureaucracy / Socialize build, minimal &quot;Oh Dragons why am I in a fight?&quot; combat skills.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T21:13:16-07:00","id":1209888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1209045#post1209045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Forest-Devil Mask makes me consider a Zorro type figure. A Dynast whose gone masked vigilante against the Realm to protect the subjugated populace of a satrapy, while maintaining their Dynast identity for intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm torn on whether the character should be a true Dynast from the Realm working in a satrapy's occupation force... or if I should make her a Cadet House member - so public collaborator, secret resistance, but closer tied the nation she's fighting for than the more broad humanitarian-motivated Realm version of the character. If I go with the Cadet House version, I'm thinking House Desai, and her secret martial arts training came from the Grass Spiders, who wanted her as their agent, but she broke away from them and they aren't happy with her either - basically making the Grass Spiders the League of Assassins/Shadows to her Batman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T23:26:16-07:00","id":1209925,"title":"","content":"I might for the fun of it 'take over' an NPC character since I think it is hilarious there is a Peleps Mizu in the Mistweaver artifact write up from Arms of the Chosen and what little we hear still leaves them almost completely blank slate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T20:32:23-07:00","id":1210257,"title":"","content":"Hmm... new idea...<br /> <br /> Ledaal Pala is convinced that anyone who thinks the House of Bells is better preparation for service to the House Legions than the Cloister of Wisdom <i>clearly hasn't spent enough time meditating on the Immaculate texts!</i> As feisty as she is idealistic, the young officer is... probably going to get somebody killed with her enthusiasm. But <i>death</i> is only a waypoint on the journey toward <i>enlightenment!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T17:36:13-07:00","id":1210698,"title":"","content":"I had a thought about a somewhat heretical character, but the design is still rough. Well Bred and a prodigy, she was accepted into the Heptegram. She successfully intiates into Sorcery soon after. The catch is, she can't tell anyone that because she has yet to exalt, so she 'washes out' after the year. She does return eventually...when her &quot;best friend&quot; (read girlfriend) has a bit of a meltdown due to her family being practically wiped out in the Battle of Futile blood. That is also when Ragara Isfrit takes the Second Breath.<br /> <br /> [Earth Aspect; Favours Bureaucracy, Lore, Melee, Occult &amp; Socialize]<br /> <br /> Loyal to her House (who protected her when she was an unExalted Sorceress, and even let her help with a Working) and is very much in love with her girlfriend (Tepet Korlei, not exactly approved by the House) but I've yet to finalize her Intimacies, as I want a better handle on who she is before I start assigning charms. Not really a fighter, but can hold her own against weenies, she is meant to play a supporting role in a Hearth, but is pretty good at leading Battle Groups and dealing with organisations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T20:11:31-07:00","id":1210777,"title":"","content":"I'm stuck in eternal Storyteller mode, which is delightful in its own way. But my next Exalted campaign is definitely gonna be a bunch of teenagers at the House of Bells, so it'll be fun to see what the PCs come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:28:10-07:00","id":1210928,"title":"","content":"After the last preview, I also want to play an Earth Immaculate wielding Faith's Pillar. It's like the devs peeked into my brain, crafted the perfect character, and then broke it out into martial arts and artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T08:38:40-07:00","id":1215803,"title":"","content":"Welp, ideas progress and concepts change. When I sat down with the full manuscript to create my original idea, I suddenly came upon a much more intriguing concept.This revelation happened as I gazed upon the control spell effects of Keel Cleaves the Clouds.<br /> <br /> So, in essence, my character is a Water Aspect sorcerer-assassin who loves the mist. I have the Artifact sword Mistweaver to produce mist. I have Keel Cleaves the Clouds as my control spell, so I can pilot a small raft on that mist and then walk on it above my mark. I have Mists of Eventide to dispatch a group of enemies or I can ambush a single opponent with Mistweaver. If I get caught, I can just disengage and try to re-establish stealth... or sic my familiar, a FRIGGIN FOGSHARK at them!<br /> <br /> Narratively she is also interesting as she is searching for her twin sister who was also trained in the arts of espionage and assassination, but vanished. Little does she know, but her sister is now a Persona-Charm using Solar of the Night Caste...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15678-cenrei","name":"Cenrei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15678_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T08:58:31-07:00","id":1215809,"title":"","content":"My upcoming DB is an Air Aspect sorceress who, at the Heptagram, plucked out her own eye to shut down the spectacularly botched summoning of a demon by a fellow student. She's a Ledaal and wants to use sorcery as her contribution to the Shadow Crusade; she has the support of her matriarch, but her mother is skeptical. That, and the general Dynastic snubbery toward sorcerers, grates on her. She's also betrothed to the group's Fire Aspect; they're both more or less asexual, but they're quite content with the situation because they just plain like each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T10:51:25-07:00","id":1215851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenrei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202695-who-will-your-next-dragon-blooded-pc-be?p=1215803#post1215803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in essence, my character is a Water Aspect sorcerer-assassin who loves the mist. I have the Artifact sword Mistweaver to produce mist. I have Keel Cleaves the Clouds as my control spell, so I can pilot a small raft on that mist and then walk on it above my mark. I have Mists of Eventide to dispatch a group of enemies or I can ambush a single opponent with Mistweaver. If I get caught, I can just disengage and try to re-establish stealth... or sic my familiar, a FRIGGIN FOGSHARK at them!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to commend you for recognizing the awesome amazingness of having a fogshark as a familiar.<br /> <br /> (Kinda building on the same idea, except my WIP character is a Suvival-supernal Solar sorcerer, who was much less subtle in my mind originally but your idea builds around mist much better, so thumbs up, and may you rock on with that one.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}